WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.867 --> 00:00:11.899
My name is Woody Hastings and I am a research professor

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:17.132
of Molecular and Cellular Biology at Harvard University in Cambridge

00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:20.332
and I want to tell a remarkable story

00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:24.166
about the discovery of quorum sensing.

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:27.366
How it came from our experiments in which

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:31.266
we discovered what we call autoinduction

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:33.632
its a more proper word perhaps

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:37.399
but quorum sensing also describes it.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.999
Now I wasn't completely concerned about it

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.499
with no objective no idea

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.599
it would ever lead to anything important

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.032
lead to anything it was just a question

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:53.332
why do cells grow exponentially

00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:57.299
and have certain processes

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:03.166
bioluminescence for one that don't turn on for 3 hours

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:09.766
then turn on very very fast so it was a basic question

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:12.832
and really this is what basic research is,

00:01:12.833 --> 00:01:18.032
is seeing phenomena I said Georgie you had seen

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:20.199
what many people have seen and

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.166
think what no one else has thought

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:29.766
is idea of discovery it is also called non-directive research

00:01:29.767 --> 00:01:32.032
it means no one else directs it

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:33.766
doesn't mean you don't direct it,

00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:38.499
you better direct it and we directed our efforts at

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:44.299
trying to understand why these bacteria

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:48.232
didn't for many hours turn on their genes.

00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:54.799
It starts really about 10 years ago in my laboratory.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.399
I saw graphs like this

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.032
in which the cells grew exponentially

00:02:00.033 --> 00:02:03.399
note on the ordinate that the

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:09.866
scale is logarithmic whereas bioluminescence

00:02:09.867 --> 00:02:12.632
for the first 3 hours didn't rise at all

00:02:12.633 --> 00:02:17.532
well I didn't I was trying to find

00:02:17.533 --> 00:02:20.299
someone when I got phone call from

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.966
a graduate student at the University of Chicago

00:02:22.967 --> 00:02:27.232
his name was Kenneth Nealson and

00:02:27.233 --> 00:02:31.499
he said I am doing the genetics

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.599
of bioluminescence in bacteria

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.099
and I am having trouble in getting

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.166
cells to produce luciferase.

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:43.999
I said I have never thought of this experiment,

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.666
luciferase wouldn't always be there.

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:53.332
I urged him to enroll in the physiology course

00:02:53.333 --> 00:02:56.866
at the Marine Biological Laboratory in Woods Hole

00:02:56.867 --> 00:03:01.699
and we would use his spare time in the course

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:06.299
which is nonexistent of course to study this phenomena

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.832
which I was so concerned about

00:03:08.833 --> 00:03:12.499
and this graph illustrates

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:14.832
the phenomena which Nealson

00:03:14.833 --> 00:03:16.332
came to study with me and

00:03:16.333 --> 00:03:18.932
he concluded that in fact

00:03:18.933 --> 00:03:26.632
the first 3 hours there was no synthesis

00:03:26.633 --> 00:03:30.099
of messenger RNA there was no synthesis

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:33.199
of luciferase protein and there

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.499
was no activity of luciferase.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:38.166
Many alternatives to that possibility

00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:42.399
you had to we had to show that was true

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.632
and we concluded that in fact the first

00:03:45.633 --> 00:03:50.032
3 hours was a time in which the cells

00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:52.699
were producing a substance which

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:59.732
was then responsible for the synthesis

00:03:59.733 --> 00:04:03.099
of messenger RNA for luciferase

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:06.366
that substance was an inducer

00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:09.366
and we said this is autoinduction its doing

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:12.166
it all by itself you don't have to add

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:15.266
anything to get any cells

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:23.266
and we took medium after cells removed

00:04:23.267 --> 00:04:27.099
the cells and we had medium that had been used

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:31.599
for growing a batch of cells

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:34.799
and we showed that we could isolate

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:40.799
from that media a substance that would

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:46.099
cause cells at low density to emit light.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:50.066
Well that was confirmed beautifully

00:04:50.067 --> 00:04:54.432
by Abrhard and Nealson

00:04:54.433 --> 00:04:59.166
in later experiments. Abrhard a decade

00:04:59.167 --> 00:05:05.266
following our publication of the

00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:09.166
original paper was able to work out

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:12.732
the structure of the autoinducer

00:05:12.733 --> 00:05:18.032
to be homoserine lactone shown here

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:24.232
and to show that in fact different

00:05:24.233 --> 00:05:28.099
chain lengths were used by specific bacteria

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:32.932
to act as autoinducers

00:05:32.933 --> 00:05:36.266
and they would not respond.

00:05:36.267 --> 00:05:42.299
Peter Greenberg became involved in this

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:47.132
and showed that very importantly that cells

00:05:47.133 --> 00:05:54.599
could communicate with other species

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:58.932
by different chain lengths

00:05:58.933 --> 00:06:04.532
of homoserine lactone like this.

00:06:04.533 --> 00:06:11.199
So having this molecule identified

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:14.566
he went on to synthesis it and made it

00:06:14.567 --> 00:06:18.132
available to Ken Nealson who with his group was

00:06:18.133 --> 00:06:20.599
able to do the definitive experiment

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:24.799
to show what we had shown with spent medium

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:32.766
he showed with pure synthesized autoinducer

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:34.832
and here is the way he did it

00:06:34.833 --> 00:06:38.199
It’s a funny graph and you have to study it a little bit

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:42.966
but he put it in a chemostat to cause cells

00:06:42.967 --> 00:06:46.399
to be fixed in a certain cell density

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.132
and as the cells got down to a certain

00:06:49.133 --> 00:06:53.999
cell density their biolumenicesece just turned off

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:59.566
and then at that point they get

00:06:59.567 --> 00:07:04.166
the cell density at this level they get the

00:07:04.167 --> 00:07:09.199
useful concentration and then added autoinducer

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:15.699
they added no more glycero. The cells responded

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:18.399
by immediately synthesizing luciferase

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:21.332
even though they were very few in number.

00:07:21.333 --> 00:07:23.999
There is no quarrel there I can assure you.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.066
This summarizes what I think the

00:07:27.067 --> 00:07:37.466
fact that the phenomena was established

00:07:37.467 --> 00:07:41.932
by 1980 you were very clearly that

00:07:41.933 --> 00:07:48.966
bioluminescent bacteria luciferase

00:07:48.967 --> 00:07:53.032
was stimulated by virtue of a substance

00:07:53.033 --> 00:07:55.932
in the media produced by the cells themselves.

00:07:55.933 --> 00:08:02.466
Many people did not agree

00:08:02.467 --> 00:08:03.866
with this conclusion.

00:08:03.867 --> 00:08:08.666
They thought it was some quirky phenomenon

00:08:08.667 --> 00:08:12.366
associated with luminescent bacteria

00:08:12.367 --> 00:08:16.166
and didn't apply to bacteriology

00:08:16.167 --> 00:08:17.966
in general to bacteria in general.

00:08:17.967 --> 00:08:25.666
By 1990 as outlined in Bonnie Bassler's

00:08:25.667 --> 00:08:29.199
beautiful expose in this series

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:33.932
this turned out

00:08:33.933 --> 00:08:40.166
she and others showed that genes responsible

00:08:40.167 --> 00:08:42.999
for this phenomena were present in all kinds

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:50.066
of bacteria and they are especially important in disease bacteria

00:08:50.067 --> 00:08:52.832
for the production of toxic substances

00:08:52.833 --> 00:08:56.299
was regulated by autoinduction

00:08:56.300 --> 00:09:02.132
But how did the name quorum sensing

00:09:02.133 --> 00:09:06.132
displace autoinduction for this phenomenon.

00:09:06.133 --> 00:09:08.832
It is described by Pete Greenberg

00:09:08.833 --> 00:09:12.166
as occurring at a dinner where he

00:09:12.167 --> 00:09:14.432
and several colleague were discussing the

00:09:14.433 --> 00:09:17.899
phenomena with other non-scientists

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:20.299
and one of the non-scientists

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:22.166
who happened to be a lawyer of course

00:09:22.167 --> 00:09:25.166
said ahah that phenomena

00:09:25.167 --> 00:09:27.732
is really a quorum sensing

00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:29.699
only when the bacteria get to a

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:34.232
certain level in culture,

00:09:34.233 --> 00:09:37.032
when there is enough autoinducer

00:09:37.033 --> 00:09:39.499
produced to cause the phenomena

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.532
we will just call it quorum sensing

00:09:41.533 --> 00:09:43.499
and he introduced the term

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:49.266
Greenberg did and from then on its history.

00:09:49.267 --> 00:09:52.232
It has turned out to be extraordinarily

00:09:52.233 --> 00:09:56.266
important in many different disease states

00:09:56.267 --> 00:10:06.332
biofilms utilize autoinduction toxic cells noxious species.

00:10:06.333 --> 00:10:10.299
The toxin is regulated by

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:13.032
autoinduction like quorum sensing.

00:10:13.033 --> 00:10:15.666
Only when a quorum of cells that

00:10:15.667 --> 00:10:18.432
is a lot of cells have infected the

00:10:18.433 --> 00:10:25.666
body of the organism you let’s say the cells produce

00:10:25.667 --> 00:10:32.532
the toxin and cause damage and they really cause damage

00:10:32.533 --> 00:10:36.532
at this point if they produce a small

00:10:36.533 --> 00:10:41.232
amount of the toxin with time,

00:10:41.233 --> 00:10:44.766
that would in fact defeat the purpose

00:10:44.767 --> 00:10:47.266
because the organism would if you will

00:10:47.267 --> 00:10:49.732
in some sense or in some way sense

00:10:49.733 --> 00:10:53.799
the presence of these bacteria

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:56.432
and raise defense against it.

00:10:56.433 --> 00:11:00.132
This illustrates that basic research

00:11:00.133 --> 00:11:03.799
can lead to phenomena and does lead to phenomena.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.832
This is only one of many examples

00:11:05.833 --> 00:11:14.132
that will lead to results that will have very very

00:11:14.133 --> 00:11:21.567
important applications such as autoinduction does. Thank you very much.

